        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0287" n="193" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg193"/>

                <head>No. 156.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Denby</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-03-01"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 1,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 164.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information copies of
                    the below-enumerated correspondence, showing that American residents in China
                    returning home on a visit, as well as travelers passing through the United
                    States, may bring with them Chinese nurses or body servants under the provisions
                    of the acts of Congress in regard to Chinese immigration.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>






